  "text": "Recipe: Korean White Radish Pancakes \u2014 Mu-Jeon\nCreator: Frank Lee\nCategory: Pancakes\nIngredients: white radish, glutinous rice flour, whole meal flour, carrot, spring onion, water\nCooking methods: boil, roast\nInstructions: Boil peeled & sliced white radish in water for 5 mins or till cooked. Drain and coat radish with 2 Tbsp glutinous rice flour in a bag. Mix 1 cup whole meal flour with 1 carrot minced, 1 spring onion minced & 1 cup water to form batter. Dip coated radish in batter and roast on non-stick pan.\nNotes: A recipe with WHOLE GRAINS (whole meal flour, glutinous rice flour), RAINBOW VEGGIES (radish, carrot, spring onion). Shared in Facebook Group: \"SANE (Sleep, Attitude, Nutrition, Exercise) for Life\"",
